# E2b del piano interlocutore-di-frontiera (§9.9): il residuo sul tabellone.
# La questione `datum` che parrot0 apre chiedendo un dato porta la condizione
# residua; una risposta con una SOGLIA («it is at most 1») la chiude se basta,
# senza imporre il valore esatto; una premessa corretta la riapre; due scopi
# non si mescolano. Banco scritto prima della cura, KB viva `agi`.
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test la soglia detta chiude l'obbligo senza il valore esatto]
!timeout 6
> calculate ready by adding arrival and transfer
> transfer is never below 0
> prefer confirming the check to asking questions when a bound settles it
> prefer explaining obstacles to asking questions when a requirement fails
> the arrival of train is 10
> for train the ready must be at most 11
> can I complete train?
<~ transfer must be at most 1
> it is at most 3
<~ at most 3
<~ transfer must be at most 1
> it is at most 1
<~ transfer is at most 1
<~ satisfied
<~ ready is at most 11
> what is the transfer of train?
<~ at most 1
<! missing
> what is the ready of train?
<~ at least 10
<~ at most 11

[test la premessa corretta riapre l'obbligo, e la stessa questione risponde all'ellissi]
!timeout 6
> for train the ready must be at most 10
> can I complete train?
<~ transfer must be at most 0
> it is 0
<~ transfer is 0
<~ satisfied
> what is the transfer of train?
<~ 0
<! at most

[test due scopi non si mescolano: la soglia risponde all'ultima domanda]
!timeout 6
> the arrival of bus is 10
> for bus the ready must be at most 12
> the arrival of cab is 10
> for cab the ready must be at most 13
> can I complete bus?
<~ transfer must be at most 2
> can I complete cab?
<~ transfer must be at most 3
> it is at most 3
<~ For cab
<~ satisfied
> can I complete bus?
<~ What is the transfer of bus?
> what remains for cab?
<~ Settled

[test la soglia detta per esteso, e il valore esatto detto dopo la sostituisce]
!timeout 6
> the arrival of tram is 10
> for tram the ready must be at least 12
> the transfer of tram is at least 2
<~ at least 2
> can I complete tram?
<~ satisfied
<~ ready is at least 12
> the transfer of tram is 1
> can I complete tram?
<~ No: ready reaches 11
> what is the transfer of tram?
<~ 1
<! at least

[test la soglia in italiano, ellittica]
!timeout 10
> per x il y deve essere al massimo z means for x the y must be at most z
> il y di x vale z means the y of x is z
> vale al massimo z means it is at most z
> il arrival di van vale 10
> per van il ready deve essere al massimo 11
> posso completare van?
<~ transfer
> vale al massimo 1
<~ at most 1
<~ van
<~ satisfied
> forget that vale al massimo z means it is at most z
> forget that per x il y deve essere al massimo z means for x the y must be at most z
> forget that il y di x vale z means the y of x is z
